169:### 6. Dependence relations and validated schedules
171:**Evidenced for Tix; Typed lifting is conjectural.** Separate a description of computation from its schedule. An affine region supplies domains and access relations indexed by iteration points. Compose access-to-location relations to compute conflicts and constrain them by original order, alias information and the relevant dependence classes. A legal time map preserves strict lexicographic order for every ordered dependence. Parallel placement requires a stronger independence condition for points in the same concurrent band or a correct synchronization/visibility proof. Preserve reduction event order for strict IEEE arithmetic. Size-dependent guards must be sufficient over the entire selected domain, including tails, zero extents, and integer bounds. [Feautrier, Affine Scheduling Part II](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01379404), [Ragan-Kelley et al., Decoupling Algorithms from Schedules](https://dspace.mit.edu/entities/publication/121e12b2-928b-4e8f-a78a-79f44d11cc6b).
174:AffineRegion { parameters, statementDomains, affineAccesses, effectSummary, originalOrder }
180:Apply this to T3's fusion boundary and T6's split, reorder and tiling. The smallest useful interface returns a precise dependence or a reason for refusal on pointwise and two-dimensional affine examples. Take both order and movement out of `planFusion`. The schedule pass selects a partition and records variants. The emitter interprets that artifact. Keep the current read-name graph as a cheap query for simple transformations. Use region scoping so a schedule artifact can reference its semantic revision and region without duplicating the entire AST. For a second domain, try one Typed affine counted-loop region from the corrected loop forest, with explicit noalias and trap facts. The loop-header fix itself is CFG theory. It does not establish affine legality. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:83`, `src/tensor/fusion.ts:142`, `T6-D/src/tensor/schedule.ts:580`, `T6-H/src/tensor/schedule.ts:522`, `src/typed/analyses.ts:215`.
