## The proposed standard library: its layering criteria and its primitives

Organize the project around a small execution framework and an independently usable compiler standard library. The framework owns the meaning of accepting, publishing, and inspecting a transformation. The library owns algorithms with reusable specifications over graphs, values, constraints, events, or measurements. Domains supply the semantics that make a particular application correct. Use "'`src/stdlib/` as the proposed location. The sketches below specify the boundaries, with directory packaging deferred until two real consumers exercise them.

### Layering criteria

| Owner | Rule for placement | Application to this review |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Framework** | Put a mechanism here when different participants must agree on its semantics for composition to work. The invariant should hold as compiler algorithms are exchanged. | Artifact identity and views, transactions and named roots, typed ports and transformation receipts, versioned analysis registration and invalidation, correspondence and obligation schemas, effect capabilities, publication, cache dependency checks, and the semantics of strategy operators. The current `dataflow()` adapter'"'s revision, encoding and transfer protocol belong on this side of the boundary. "'`src/framework/ir/view.ts:53`, `src/framework/ir/transactions.ts:294`, `src/framework/contracts/analysis-manager.ts:227`, `src/framework/dataflow/analysis.ts:120`, `src/framework/dataflow/analysis.ts:160`, `src/framework/strategy/interpreter.ts:134`. |
